        "SiteFields": {
            "description": "Site columns as schema XML, matched by internal name (Name). A missing one is created; one the web has gets the template merged onto its stored schema, written only when that changes something, so what the template leaves out (an index, a formatter, a description) survives. A widening type change is applied, another type change is a warning and leaves it as it is. A new target (a lookup's list, a taxonomy column's term set or term store) is a warning that keeps the stored one, unless the column was made in this setup. A column SharePoint refuses is logged as an error and the others still run. Changes do not reach the column's existing list copies.",
